---
description: Vue reactivity usage
globs: *.ts
alwaysApply: false
---
The project uses Vue 3 reactivity even for server-side state:
- Use watchEffect for reactive responses to state changes
- Structure files with composable patterns
- Prefer computed values over repeated calculations
- All player state changes should be reactive to propagate correctly to client/UI
- Never mutate reactive objects outside their defining scope (e.g. only server can mutate user, character and game-state stores, while client can only mutate client store)
